# Fail fast (no silent defensive coding by default)

Aligns with [`python-services-rules`](https://github.com/drivestream-lab/python-services-rules)
`fail-fast.mdc` intent.

## Prefer

- Surface invalid config, broken invariants, and impossible state immediately
  (`Result`, typed errors) — do not paper over with defaults.
- Handle retries only at explicit infra boundaries with policy (documented).

## Avoid without approval

- Broad catch-all that swallows errors or substitutes silent defaults.
- Defensive branches for types already validated at the boundary.

Document approved exceptions in an ADR (**`rust-device-adr.mdc`**).

## Related rules

- **Typing at edges:** validate config/IPC at boundaries
- **Logging:** `logging-observability.mdc`
